t you are giving your opinion and not stating a fact. An opinion is your personal view or belief about something. Whereas a fact refers to something real or true and is supported by evidence or documentation.</ns0:t></ns0:r><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Gill Sans Nova" ns0:hAnsi="Gill Sans Nova" /><ns0:lang ns0:val="en-US" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve"> </ns0:t></ns0:r><ns0:r ns0:rsidRPr="00EF5E37"><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Gill Sans Nova" ns0:hAnsi="Gill Sans Nova" /><ns0:lang ns0:val="en-US" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">It’s important to clearly state what you are saying is your opinion and not fact. </ns0:t></ns0:r><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Gill Sans Nova" ns0:hAnsi="Gill Sans Nova" /><ns0:lang ns0:val="en-US" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t>Opinion phrases</ns0:t></ns0:r><ns0:r ns0:rsidRPr="00EF5E37"><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Gill Sans Nova" ns0:hAnsi="Gill Sans Nova" /><ns0:lang ns0:val="en-US" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve"> make it clear to the listener that you are giving your opinion, and not stating a proven fact.</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p></ns0:txbxContent></ns1:textbox><ns4:wrap anchorx="page" anchory="page" /></ns1:roundrect></ns0:pict>